#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand why the Ubuntu installer asks you to deactivate BitLocker, and "
"what you can do before installing Ubuntu alongside Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:8
msgid "Topics: Installation Security Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:12
msgid "BitLocker during Ubuntu installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:14
msgid ""
"During the installation type step, the Ubuntu installer might inform you "
"that you can't proceed without first deactivating Windows BitLocker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:16
msgid ""
"![The BitLocker is enabled page](/images/installer/bitlocker-is-enabled.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:16
msgid "The BitLocker is enabled page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:19
msgid "BitLocker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:21
msgid ""
"BitLocker Drive Encryption is a data protection feature that integrates with "
"the Windows operating system. When activated, it will encrypt the contents "
"of the hard drives in Windows, making the data inaccessible without the "
"correct decryption key. It is designed to minimize the risk of data theft or "
"exposure from lost or stolen computers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:23
msgid ""
"When a user starts their computer and properly authenticates with the "
"correct credentials, BitLocker decrypts the data and allows seamless usage "
"of the hard drive and the data that it contains. Without the correct "
"credentials, the encrypted hard drive data looks like random noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:25
msgid "BitLocker and Ubuntu installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:27
msgid ""
"If you plan to install Ubuntu side by side with Windows, you need to take "
"into consideration the operational setup on your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:29
msgid ""
"If you are not using BitLocker, Ubuntu can see the correct hard drive "
"structure, including any partitions and data stored on it. The guided "
"installer can correctly map the data and safely install Ubuntu alongside "
"Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:31
msgid ""
"If you are using BitLocker, the hard drive content isn't accessible, and it "
"appears as random noise. The Ubuntu installer can't correctly map data, and "
"can't install alongside Windows without data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:33
msgid ""
"Additionally, some manufacturers ship systems with BitLocker enabled but the "
"hard drive content not yet encrypted. In this case, the Ubuntu installer "
"also can't correctly map data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:35
msgid "What you can do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:37
msgid "Cancel the installation of Ubuntu and continue using Windows only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:39
msgid ""
"Decide that the data stored in Windows is not important, and that you are "
"willing to overwrite the data contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:41
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu installer can then erase the entire contents of the hard drive "
"and create its own structure (partitions and data)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:43
msgid ""
"This is a destructive operation, with no option to recover any Windows data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:45
msgid "Decide to turn BitLocker off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:47
msgid ""
"This will turn off the encryption feature. The hard drive and its data will "
"be visible and accessible from the Ubuntu installer, allowing it to safely "
"set up a side-by-side configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:49
msgid "For details, see {ref}`turn-off-bitlocker-in-windows`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:52
msgid ""
"Certain versions of Windows will no longer allow you to re-enable BitLocker "
"after disabling it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/bitlocker-during-ubuntu-installation.md:54
msgid ""
"If you wish to re-encrypt your Windows partition after installing Ubuntu "
"alongside it, check that your version of Windows supports this."
msgstr ""
